+## Item 4: talker starts (#667)
+
+**Method.** This is lane B13's run ([667_TALKER_START_BENCH.md](667_TALKER_START_BENCH.md)) with B13's controller probe.
+The probe was rebuilt from the same library source (export hash `23ac438f`, B13's).
+Each start binds the DUT's STREAM_OUTPUT 0 (AAF) to the peer's STREAM_INPUT 0, under the binding rule.
+It holds 2,000 ms from the bind response and polls the peer's counters at 20, 100 and 250 ms, then every 500 ms.
+Then it unbinds and reads again after 1,200 ms.
+Three captures run around each start: the brief's untagged AVTP and the tagged AVTP on the tap, and the controller's AVDECC frames.
+
+**Result.** All 100 binds and unbinds succeeded.
+EARLY_TIMESTAMP and LATE_TIMESTAMP stayed 0 in every start.
+The application error rule raised no increment.
+The first-to-second presentation-time step was 124,999 ns in 66 starts, 125,000 ns in 26, 125,019 ns in 6 and 125,020 ns in 2.
+That is within 21 ns of the steady period.
+All 1,000 initial headers carry `tv=1` and `tu=0`, and no start has a sequence gap.
+B13 counted 14 EARLY starts out of 100 on dev `28f9666f`, each with a backward first step of -544 to -280 ms.
+That startup behaviour did not occur in 100 starts on this image.
+Absolute gPTP correlation is NOT RUN, as in B13.
