+## Item 5: default map and two-hour soak (#682, #658)
+
+**Default map.** GET_AUDIO_MAP read the DUT's maps at 05:17 UTC, the first ATDECC read after the identity gate, before this lane changed anything.
+
+- STREAM_PORT_INPUT 0 holds 4 mappings: stream channels 0 to 3 to clusters 0 to 3, channel 0.
+- STREAM_PORT_OUTPUT 0 holds 8 mappings: stream channels 0 to 7 to clusters 0 to 7, channel 0.
+
+The maps read the same at 05:45, 06:22 and 08:23.
+#658 had found 1 of 4 input mappings and an empty output map.
+Both maps equal the identity default #658 ruled, clipped to the 4-channel input format: stream channel c to cluster c for every c below the smaller of the format's channel count and the port's cluster count ([ruling](https://github.com/kebag-logic/milan-fpga/issues/658#issuecomment-5988293154) item 1; [rulings](https://github.com/kebag-logic/milan-fpga/issues/658#issuecomment-5988843004) items 1 and 3).
+The read is the effective map.
+The DUT's saved state then held 54 records (image sequence 234), so a saved mapping cannot be excluded by this read.
+
+**Soak.** The soak started at 06:23:22 UTC and ran 7,200.5 s.
+It used B13's four bindings, each under the binding rule:
+
+- the peer's AAF to the DUT's STREAM_INPUT 0;
+- the peer's CRF to the DUT's STREAM_INPUT 1;
+- the DUT's AAF to the peer's STREAM_INPUT 0;
+- the DUT's CRF to the peer's STREAM_INPUT 8.
+
+The last two were in place as found.
+The DUT stayed at INTERNAL, and the peer followed the DUT's CRF, as found.
+The cadence is B13's: GET_COUNTERS every 60 s (121 polls), GET_AVB_INFO and GET_AS_PATH every 5 minutes (25 reads), and a rolling tap.
+The polls read nine descriptors.
+B13's probe observed the unsolicited counter notifications under the application's error rule.
+
+**Result: PASS.**
+
+- No error-class counter increased at any poll: MEDIA_UNLOCKED, STREAM_INTERRUPTED, SEQ_NUM_MISMATCH, UNSUPPORTED_FORMAT, LATE_TIMESTAMP and EARLY_TIMESTAMP on every listener; STREAM_STOP, MEDIA_RESET and TIMESTAMP_UNCERTAIN on both DUT talkers; LINK_DOWN and GPTP_GM_CHANGED; CLOCK_DOMAIN UNLOCKED.
+- The application rule raised no increment.
+- The grandmaster, asCapable and the AS path did not change at any timing read.
+- FRAMES_RX advanced by 57,599,387 on the DUT's STREAM_INPUT 0, one per PDU (see the observations below).
+  On the peer it advanced by 57,599,253 for the DUT's AAF and 3,599,953 for its CRF.
+- On the tap, summed over the 121 tagged-AVTP captures, whose spans total 6,858.7 s including their overlaps and the 16 s before t0, the four streams carried 54,869,021 and 54,869,000 AAF PDUs and 3,429,307 and 3,429,316 CRF PDUs.
+  None has an `mr` toggle, `tv=0` or `tu=1`.
+- Three captures each lose a burst within 45 ms of their first frame.
+  Captures 002 and 042 lose PDUs on all four streams, capture 035 on three: the DUT's CRF stream lost nothing there.
+  Each affected AAF stream lost 9 to 12 PDUs and each affected CRF stream 1.
+  The overlapping previous capture holds every missing PDU, so the loss is in the capture path.
+- All 363 captures report no dropped packets in the capture statistics.
+  The tap covered 6,823.7 s of the 7,200.5 s; the 16 gaps of 12 to 44 s fall between foreground chunks.
+  The counters span them.
+
+**Observations, not error-class counters.**
+
+- **The DUT's two listeners count FRAMES_RX under different laws.** Milan v1.2 Table 5.4 (FRAMES_TX) and Table 5.6 (FRAMES_RX) define observation-interval counters.
+  Each advances by one at the end of every interval, at most 1 s long, in which at least one stream data PDU was transmitted or received.
+  FRAMES_TX on both DUT talkers advanced by exactly 7,200 in 7,200 s, the one-per-interval count `hdl/ieee1722/avtp/KL_talker_diag_ctx.sv` declares.
+  FRAMES_RX on the DUT's CRF listener, STREAM_INPUT 1, also advanced by 7,200.
+  Its server is `hdl/ieee1722/crf/KL_crf_rx.sv`, which counts intervals with at least one accepted PDU (`:233`; GET_COUNTERS FRAMES_RX at `hdl/milan/milan_datapath.sv:3701`).
+  FRAMES_RX on the DUT's AAF listener, STREAM_INPUT 0, advanced by 57,599,387 in 7,200.5 s: about 8,000 per second, one per PDU.
+  That is the law `hdl/ieee1722/avtp/KL_avtp_rx_monitor_ctx.sv` declares and implements for the AAF listeners: each interval commit adds the interval's frame total, under a ruling of 2026-08-05 (`:318-323` and `:627-630`).
+  The header of the same file (`:28-36`) says each interval moves the counter by at most one, so the repository's declarations conflict.
+  `tests/features/counters_contract_milan.feature` describes Table 5.6's reading as one per interval (`:194-201`), and grades a per-frame FRAMES_RX advance under Table 5.6 as INFO, not FAIL (`:393-408`).
+  The reference peer's FRAMES_RX also advanced once per PDU, by 57,599,253 for the DUT's AAF and 3,599,953 for its CRF.
+  For triage: whether the frame-total law conforms to Table 5.6, and which of the repository's conflicting declarations governs.
+- **No unsolicited STREAM_INPUT counters from the DUT.** One soak minute's control capture holds 60 unsolicited GET_COUNTERS for each DUT STREAM_OUTPUT, one per second.
+  It holds none for either DUT STREAM_INPUT, although FRAMES_RX on input 0 changed throughout.
+  Milan v1.2 Sections 5.4.5.1 and 5.4.5.2 (Table 5.22) send a changed counter unsolicited, rate-limited to one per second.
+  So the application error rule saw only the peer's two listeners, 6,909 notifications each.
+  The DUT's listeners are graded by the direct polls above. This needs triage.
+- **Two loopback slips in the soak configuration.** The DUT was at INTERNAL, receiving a peer stream that follows the DUT's own CRF.
+  `SLIP_LB` stepped by one frame across the soak's own bind.
+  It read `0x8e` at 06:22:39.06 and `0x90` at 06:23:23.21, the first soak read.
+  The peer's AAF talker was bound to the DUT's STREAM_INPUT 0 at 06:22:39.51, and the soak's t0 is 06:23:22.71.
+  So the step lies between 0.45 s before the bind and 0.50 s after t0: before the graded soak, unless it fell in its first 0.50 s.
+  The records cannot place it more exactly.
+  It stepped by one more frame between 06:28:23 and 06:33:23, 5 to 10 minutes into the soak, and was static for the remaining 110 minutes.
+  A bind is not among the settle recentre's arm terms: a CLOCK_SOURCE change, an aligner re-engagement or an aligner excursion ([MEDIA_CLOCK_FOLLOWING.md](../design/MEDIA_CLOCK_FOLLOWING.md#settle-recentre)).
+  Whether any recentre fired after this bind is not observable, because no register counts it.
+  The declared transient covers source changes and aligner pull-ins, not this case.
+  The records do not show the cause; both slips are for triage under #645 and #647.
+  `RENDER_STAT`'s rail count stayed 10 and `SLIP_TDM` 0 throughout.
+
+## Item 6: Ethernet receive sanity (#691)
+
+**Link: PASS.** `MAC_STATUS` read `0x0000000d` at all 27 console reads from 06:22 to 08:23 UTC: link up, 1000 Mb/s, full duplex.
+The AVB_INTERFACE counters held LINK_UP 1, LINK_DOWN 0 and GPTP_GM_CHANGED 0 over the soak.
+gPTP read `SYNC=1 ASCAPABLE=1 TU=0` at every read, with the grandmaster equal to the parent.
+
+**Receive error counters: NOT RUN.**
+
+- The DUT's AVB_INTERFACE counters carry LINK_UP, LINK_DOWN and GPTP_GM_CHANGED only (valid mask `0x23`), with no RX_CRC_ERROR.
+- `STATS_CAP` read `0x1B8` ([REGISTER_MAP.md](../reference/REGISTER_MAP.md#0x200-----statistics-rmon--req-mac-04)).
+  On this build the RMON lanes for FCS errors (`0x224`), preamble or alignment errors (`0x220`) and frames delivered flagged bad (`0x22C`) are real.
+  Receive drops have no source: lane 6, `RX_FIFO_OVERFLOW` at `0x228`, has `STATS_CAP` bit 6 = 0, and the register map says such a lane must be rendered "not supported" by software, never "0 errors".
+- Every lane at `0x210` to `0x230` read zero at every read, which the register map defines as "no valid snapshot".
+  A snapshot needs a `STATS_CTRL[0]` write, and this lane's rules allow no register write beyond the stream and audio-interface controls.
+- So the FCS and alignment counts are NOT RUN here, and this build has no receive-drop count to read.
+
+As an end-to-end indication only, the DUT's two listeners counted no SEQ_NUM_MISMATCH and no STREAM_INTERRUPTED over the soak, 57.6 million AAF PDUs among them.
+That is not the FCS or alignment count the item asks for.
+
+## Item 7: MAAP interoperation (#686)
+
+**The DUT's state.** Every console read from 05:20 to 08:23 UTC is the same.
+
+- `MAAP_CTRL` read `0x00000201`: enabled, 2 addresses.
+- `MAAP_STAT0` read `0x0000DD85`: 0 conflicts, 0 DEFENDs sent, offset `0xDD85`.
+- `MAAP_STAT1` read `0x00000006`: ANNOUNCE, address valid.
+
+The DUT holds `91:E0:F0:00:DD:85` and the next address.
+
+**On the tap (PASS for what is observable).** The soak's untagged-AVTP captures hold 879 MAAP PDUs, over 6,780.9 s of coverage.
+
+- The DUT sent 220 ANNOUNCEs for that one range, all to `91:E0:F0:00:FF:00`.
+  127 intervals fall inside covered spans; they measure 30.505 to 31.405 s, mean 31.004 s.
+  IEEE 1722-2016 Annex B.3.4.1 bounds the announce interval strictly between 30 and 32 s.
+  [MAAP_FABRIC.md](../design/MAAP_FABRIC.md#annex-b-contract) declares a draw of 30.488 to 31.511 s.
+- The reference peer announced two single-address ranges, `91:E0:F0:00:17:11` and `91:E0:F0:00:85:22`.
+- A third station on the segment announced one range of 2 addresses, `91:E0:F0:00:2F:2B`.
+- No two of the four ranges overlap.
+  No station sent a PROBE or a DEFEND, and the DUT counted no conflict.
+
+**NOT RUN.** The DUT's acquisition, its PROBEs and their timing, ran at its last cold boot.
+This lane may not reset or power-cycle anything.
+A DEFEND needs a PROBE that overlaps the DUT's range, and none occurred.
+So the DEFEND destination and conflict fields are not exercised on the bench.
