+## Item 8: restore
+
+**As found.** Before item 2, the DUT was at INTERNAL with both listeners unbound.
+The peer's STREAM_INPUT 0 held the DUT's AAF talker and its STREAM_INPUT 8 the DUT's CRF talker, both with flags `0x0082`.
+The peer's clock source was 1, its INPUT_STREAM source on STREAM_INPUT 8.
+Lanes B2, B8 and B13 started from all listeners unbound and the peer at INTERNAL.
+
+**Read back.** Every change was undone and read back.
+
+- Items 2 and 3 each set the peer's clock source to 0 and restored 1. Item 2 read 1 at 05:45:36; item 3 read 1 at 06:08:53.
+- Item 4 released the peer's STREAM_INPUT 0 binding and re-bound it under the binding rule; it read back with flags `0x0082`.
+- The soak's two peer-to-DUT bindings were released at 08:23.
+
+The as-found reads of 05:17 to 05:20 give 15 rows: 7 stream formats, both clock sources, 4 listener states (the peer's STREAM_INPUT 0 and 8 and the DUT's two inputs) and the DUT's two maps.
